+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+The end-to-end, full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` hook had a measured p95 of
+**10.27 ms** on the adversarial synthetic corpus built from a 30-word
+vocabulary.
+
+The term-selection fix discarded terms whose document frequency was greater
+than one third of the active records, then selected at most the eight remaining
+terms with the highest IDF. The synthetic generator was also changed to a Zipf
+distribution: 30 frequent domain words plus 2,000 rare identifiers, avoiding a
+corpus in which every record contained every query term.
+
+After that change, the measured end-to-end, full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` p95
+was **1.82 ms**.
